telegram-desktop (7.3.0+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.3.0. This is the first upload since 7.2.9: 7.2.10
    updated emoji to Unicode 17, plays the audio tracks of a rich message as
    a playlist, submits the rich messages editor with Ctrl+Enter and improves
    screen reader support; 7.3's changelog reads only "Money.": it adds an
    in-app TON wallet, with gram transfers in chats.
  * Build-depend on libtdesktop-rust-dev instead of libtlottie-dev. 7.3.0
    links its Rust dependencies, tlottie and the new wallet-engine, as one
    static library, libtdesktop_rust, and compiles wallet-engine's generated
    C++ binding itself. Versioned at the first upload carrying 7.3.0's pins,
    since a static library with no SONAME gives nothing else to stop a build
    against an older archive.
  * Build-depend on libtgowt-dev (>= 0~git20261007.d1cf250+ppa1~resolute1),
    7.3.0's new tg_owt pin, versioned for the same reason.
  * No other packaging changes. The new updater code is compiled out by
    DESKTOP_APP_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE, so it needs no LZMA; zxcvbn-c is
    vendored and built in-tree; the Qt 6.10 accessibility patch still
    applies.
  * The tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Fri, 09 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.2.9+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.2.9: tlottie rendering fixes, plus a sweep of leak,
    retain-cycle and use-after-free fixes.
  * Build-depend on libtlottie-dev (>= 0~git20260911.31f1b54+ppa1~resolute1),
    the first carrying 7.2.9's tlottie pin and its patch. Versioned because
    tlottie is a static library with no SONAME, so nothing else would stop a
    build against the older, unpatched archive.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Thu, 17 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.2.8+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.2.8. This is the first upload since 7.2.5: 7.2.6
    brought a text tool with fonts, alignment and styles in the image editor,
    dropping folders and file sets into a chat to send as one archive,
    editing GIFs before sending with a caption, and rating a finished call
    from the call panel; 7.2.7 fixed crashes with invalid lottie files; 7.2.8
    adds Qt RHI diagnostics logging and fixes a media-viewer vertex buffer
    under-allocation. A 7.2.7 changelog entry was prepared but never
    uploaded, and is dropped rather than kept as history for a version that
    could not have built.
  * Build-depend on libtlottie-dev, new in this PPA. Upstream 7.2.7 replaced
    the bundled rlottie with dkaraush/tlottie, a Rust rewrite with a C API,
    and cmake/external/tlottie does an unconditional find_library on Linux.
    That is what the 7.2.7 attempt missed.
  * Drop the Telegram/ThirdParty/rlottie gitlink and the lintian override for
    its vendored RapidJSON licence. Upstream deleted the submodule in 7.2.7;
    the gitlink survived as rebase debris and put 14 MB of dead source into
    the tarball, and the override now fires as unused.
  * Add libpango1.0-dev to Build-Depends, also new in 7.2.7.
    cmake/external/pango does an ungated pkg_check_modules(... REQUIRED
    pangocairo), and DESKTOP_APP_USE_PANGO defaults to ON on Linux.
  * No other packaging changes. The QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH
    workarounds still apply, cld3 still needs no protoc, and the Qt 6.10
    accessibility patch still applies.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Thu, 10 Sep 2026 22:10:00 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.2.5+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release 7.2.5, skipping the 7.2.6 pre-release.
  * The whole 7.2.x series concerns upstream's v2 update system — a rotated
    then revoked signing key, and finally a new autoupdate manifest source.
    None of it affects this package, which is built with
    DESKTOP_APP_DISABLE_AUTOUPDATE=ON and is updated through the PPA instead.
  * Includes the 7.1.5 Linux crash fix ("Destroy main window on X11 on
    explicit hide only", bea90214ec). The 7.2 branch forked on 28 August,
    before 7.1.5 shipped on 2 September, so this was verified rather than
    assumed: the commit is an ancestor of v7.2.5.
  * No packaging changes. Only the lib_base submodule moved; cld3 still needs
    no protoc, the QSB_EXECUTABLE and GI_GIR_PATH workarounds still apply, the
    Qt 6.10 accessibility patch still applies, and the set of required
    external dependencies is unchanged.
  * The tg_owt, tde2e and rnnoise pins are unchanged.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Fri, 04 Sep 2026 13:36:20 +0000

