telegram-desktop (7.0.7+ppa2~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Anchor the debian/source/options tar-ignore patterns. They are passed to
    tar --exclude, which matches any path component when the pattern has no
    slash, so an unanchored "build" also removed Telegram/build/ from the
    source tarball. That directory holds the version file read by
    cmake/version.cmake, and every architecture failed configure on Launchpad
    as a result.

 -- Stanislav Aleksandrov <lightofmysoul@gmail.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 21:40:00 +0000

telegram-desktop (7.0.7+ppa1~resolute1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging for ppa:lightofmysoul/tg.
  * Built from upstream tag v7.0.7 with every submodule in place, so the
    bundled fonts, libprisma grammars and patched rlottie upstream expects are
    used rather than substituted.
  * Links our libtgowt-dev, libtde2e-dev and librnnoise-dev, none of which
    exist in Ubuntu.
  * Uses the API credentials upstream publishes in snap/snapcraft.yaml.
  * Autoupdate and crash reporting disabled.

